        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-24 23:07:22.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21322 lfsck: keep a partial namespace LFSCK idle",
        "message": "LU-21322 lfsck: keep a partial namespace LFSCK idle\n\nWhen a namespace LFSCK finished with an MDT that failed or did not\njoin it, its status was LS_PARTIAL, which lfsck_namespace_setup() did\nnot know. On the next mount it printed \"unknown lfsck_namespace status\n8\" and set the status to LS_CRASHED, so the MDT restarted the LFSCK\nwhen recovery completed. lfsck_namespace_prep() reset only a completed\nLFSCK, so that run and any later start without \"-r\" kept LF_INCOMPLETE\nand were partial again, on every mount.\n\nKeep a partial namespace LFSCK idle and start it from the beginning,\nas layout LFSCK does. Resume a namespace LFSCK that its controller\nfailed, stopped or paused, as layout LFSCK does, without the message.\n\nsanity-lfsck test_28b remounts an MDT whose namespace LFSCK is\npartial, checks that it does not start again, then starts it without\n\"-r\" and checks that it completes. test_28 becomes test_28a.\n\nFixes: b356ff8e1bec (\"LU-4788 lfsck: namespace LFSCK uses assistant thread\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lfsck mdscount=2 mdtcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I2e70432e189346bd198307af964cd982303ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
